The three levels of the store's context
Four levels stacked. The world the system serves holds another system's FHIR
client, a jurisdiction's authority, a clinician and a person. The system built
on the store holds its screens and clinical logic and its process and step
definitions, and reaches the store embedded in the same JVM or over HTTP. The
store holds a face per FHIR version, the engine and a runtime per tenant, and
a client or a jurisdiction may reach a face directly without passing through
the system above. What the store needs is a spec per tenant, an operator for
databases and credentials, and PostgreSQL with a database per tenant.
